--Description:  We need to find seasons where more than one driver shares the top season-points total.
--              Strategy:
--              1) Aggregate points each driver scored in each season → driver_year_points.
--              2) For every season, obtain the maximum of those totals → max_driver_points.
--              3) Keep only the rows whose total equals that seasonal max and count them.
--                 • COUNT = 1 → single champion (no tie)
--                 • COUNT > 1 → tie for most points
--              Ordered by the count (biggest ties first) and limited to 20 rows for brevity.
WITH driver_year_points AS (
    SELECT r."year",
